Troubleshooting Common Issues
Issue 1: Job Template Won't Launch
Symptoms: Launch button is grayed out or missing

Solutions:

Verify inventory is properly configured and has hosts
Check that credentials are properly associated
Ensure the playbook exists in the specified project
Confirm you have proper permissions to launch jobs
Issue 2: Jobs Fail with Permission Errors
Symptoms: Tasks fail with "Permission denied" errors

Solutions:

Verify SSH credentials are correct and have proper access
Check that "Enable Privilege Escalation" is checked if using become
Ensure the SSH user has sudo privileges on target hosts
Test SSH connectivity manually from the AWX server
Issue 3: Playbook Not Found
Symptoms: "Playbook not found" error when launching

Solutions:

Verify the playbook file exists in the correct project directory
Check file permissions (should be readable by awx user)
Ensure the project is properly synced
Verify the playbook path in the job template
Issue 4: Slow Job Execution
Symptoms: Jobs take longer than expected to complete

Solutions:

Check network connectivity between AWX and managed hosts
Verify SSH connection settings and authentication
Review playbook efficiency and task complexity
Consider using connection multiplexing for better performance
Best Practices for Job Templates
Template Organization
Use descriptive names that clearly indicate the template's purpose
Include comprehensive descriptions explaining what the template does
Organize templates by function (system maintenance, application deployment, etc.)
Use consistent naming conventions across your organization
Security Considerations
Limit template access using AWX role-based access control
Use separate credentials for different environments (dev, staging, prod)
Avoid hardcoding sensitive data in playbooks; use AWX credentials instead
Regularly audit who has access to launch which templates
Performance Optimization
Use job tags to run only necessary tasks
Implement proper error handling in playbooks
Use fact caching for frequently run jobs
Consider job slicing for large inventories
